  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is to establish a clean, minimal baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) uses the simplest standard encoder (PCA-2000) on the primary modality (RNA) with the simplest profile setting. This gives a performance floor against which all other design choices (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion) can be measured. It is computationally cheap, well-understood, and isolates the RNA signal quality without confounding from additional modalities or complex aggregation. From this anchor, subsequent experiments can systematically test whether scvi/scgpt encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or multimodal fusion each add value, making the remaining 9 experiments far more interpretable."
}

